# Booking MVP isolation

## Response ritual

Every assistant reply in this project MUST start with exactly:

Помню про правила

Do this before any other text (including tool summaries).

## Goal

Build a clean MVP widget under `src/widgets/booking/`, then eventually replace `src/widgets/stepper/`. Do not break or rewrite the old widget while migrating.

## Allowed writes

- Create and edit files only under `src/widgets/booking/**`
- New styles only under `src/widgets/booking/**` (e.g. `booking.css`, colocated CSS modules)
- Minimal entry wiring only: `src/App.tsx`, `src/main.tsx`, `src/widgets/index.ts` — only to mount/export the booking widget, without changing stepper behavior

## Forbidden writes (read / import only)

- `src/widgets/stepper/**`
- `src/components/ui/**`
- `src/lib/**`
- `src/styles.css`
- `src/widgets/stepper/stepper.css`

Do not edit, refactor, delete, or “improve” these paths. If a shared UI/lib piece is needed, copy or reimplement it inside `src/widgets/booking/`.

## Migration practice

- Prefer importing reusable logic from stepper for speed, then replace with clean local versions step by step
- Do not copy the whole stepper tree into booking in one go
- Do not remove `stepper` until the user explicitly asks

## Examples

```text
❌ Edit src/components/ui/button.tsx for booking styles
✅ Create src/widgets/booking/ui/Button.tsx (or booking.css tokens)

❌ Patch stepper.css
✅ Add src/widgets/booking/booking.css

❌ “Quick fix” in StepperWidget.tsx
✅ Change only BookingWidget under src/widgets/booking/
```
